# Companies — /api/companies
#
# Run `dotnet run --project JsonApiPoc` first, then click the gutter icon next to a request.
# `###` separates requests; the text after it is the request name. "->" notes the expected outcome.
#
# Seed: 1 Acme Manufacturing (2 contacts), 2 Globex Logistics (1), 3 Initech Software (2),
#       4 Umbrella Health (no contacts).

@host = http://localhost:5031

### List companies
GET {{host}}/api/companies
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by name
GET {{host}}/api/companies?sort=name
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by industry, descending
GET {{host}}/api/companies?sort=-industry
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Second page of 2 -> links.prev/next, meta.total
GET {{host}}/api/companies?page[number]=2&page[size]=2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sparse fieldset: names only
GET {{host}}/api/companies?fields[companies]=name
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Single company -> relationships.contacts carries links.related only (links-only to-many)
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Missing company -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/companies/999
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Related resource collection: follow relationships.contacts.links.related.
# The contacts are the response's `data`, so this route pages and sorts like
# any other collection. There is no /relationships/contacts route by design.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Acme's contacts -> Jan Kowalski, Maria Nowak; meta.total 2
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1/contacts
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by last name, descending
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1/contacts?sort=-lastName
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### One per page -> a next link that keeps the nested path
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1/contacts?page[size]=1
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sparse fieldset on the related collection
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1/contacts?fields[contacts]=email
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### A company with no contacts -> 200 with data: [], meta.total 0 (not a 404)
GET {{host}}/api/companies/4/contacts
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Contacts of a missing company -> 404 (the company itself does not exist)
GET {{host}}/api/companies/999/contacts
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Query validation -> 400 problem details
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Unsupported sort field -> 400 (detail lists name, industry)
GET {{host}}/api/companies?sort=height
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unsupported sort on the related collection -> 400 (its own allowlist)
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1/contacts?sort=industry
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown query parameter -> 400 (strict validation)
GET {{host}}/api/companies?foo=bar
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Paging a single resource -> 400 (only collections paginate)
GET {{host}}/api/companies/1?page[number]=2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Companies expose no filters -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/companies?filter[industry]=Manufacturing
Accept: application/vnd.api+json
